# PINS: every pinned input of the eq-container images, one KEY=VALUE per line (parsed by build.sh --check; do not add spaces
# around '='). The same values are the global ARG defaults (`ARG KEY=VALUE` before the first FROM) of Dockerfile.minimal and
# Dockerfile.toolchains; build.sh fails (exit 2 before a build, 11 in --check) when they differ, and verify-tools.sh compares
# the tool pins with TOOLS.toml. Bases (USER decision 2026-10-06, DESIGN_DISTROLESS.md): every final image is FROM scratch or
# FROM the distroless cc image below; no Debian snapshot, apt or dpkg anywhere (the former BASE_IMAGE, APT_SNAPSHOT,
# BASE_LAYER_URL and BASE_LAYER_SHA256 keys are gone with distro-pins.sh).
#
# Placeholder rule: a value that is UNSET or contains TODO is never invented. build.sh refuses to build an image that needs
# it (exit 13) and prints the command that produces the value; whoever fills it commits the change.
# Format rules (build.sh pin_format): *_IMAGE and DISTROLESS_CC are NAME[:TAG]@sha256:<64 hex> (never a tag alone, never
# `latest`, never a `debug` variant; DISTROLESS_* only gcr.io/distroless/*-debian13), *_SHA256 are 64 lowercase hex.
# Rule for a re-pin: change the value here AND in the Dockerfile ARG default, rebuild, rerun the probe
# (eq-container.sh install --force-verify) before freezing.

# ---- builder images (discarded stages only; never in a final image). Digests from docker-library/repo-info, NOT read from
# Docker Hub (the agent cannot reach it): the builder verifies the digest when it pulls, so a wrong one fails loudly.
# buildpack-deps:trixie (repo-info c0ec1cf4, 2026-10-06; arm64 v8 manifest 5f1ada0b...): curl, git, gnupg, xz, bzip2, unzip,
# gcc, make, file, binutils; no zstd. Fetch, Mathlib and the assemble stages run on it; no apt-get runs in any stage.
BUILDER_IMAGE=buildpack-deps:trixie@sha256:47fa3fd7df8022082e3f885881775cc7927ec210b470cc4eae9e874f871b008a
# alpine:3.24 (repo-info c667a56c, 2026-09-18; arm64 v8 manifest 260479a1...): the ONE stage with a package manager, `apk add
# build-base bison gnupg curl` (signature-checked by apk, floating within 3.24) to build the static bash; its output is pinned
# by BASH_BIN_SHA256 below.
MUSL_BUILDER_IMAGE=alpine:3.24@sha256:294b683cb724975bec92580e1e685676bd4b50bda910ddb8c51d4cabeaec77e6

# ---- the final base. gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian13 tag `nonroot`: INDEX digest, and the linux/arm64 v8 manifest it lists.
# Read 2026-10-06 through the r.jina.ai reader (gcr.io is outside the agent sandbox); the bytes are kept in base/ and hash to
# these two values (the index lists the arm64 manifest; verify-tools.sh --manifest re-checks both offline): consistency, not
# authenticity. Authenticity: `bash lib/eq-container/base-pins.sh` (cosign verify, keyless identity
# keyless@distroless.iam.gserviceaccount.com, issuer https://accounts.google.com), checklist D1.
# Contents (distroless cc/config.bzl): Debian 13 libc6, libssl3t64, libzstd1, zlib1g, libgomp1, libstdc++6, libgcc-s1,
# gcc-14-base, ca-certificates, tzdata, /etc/passwd with root, nobody, nonroot (65532). No shell.
DISTROLESS_CC=gcr.io/distroless/cc-debian13@sha256:e792ab3d241a468a4fd7519ddbbebe66b49b5f365771716ea688ad40b6c6f1c2
DISTROLESS_CC_ARM64=sha256:2f0295ce228a23109ec1c8d38763bfe995b0dba7b3672f58d3a67ebfbc542fdc

